window.QBANK = [{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Kinematics","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"A car starts from rest and accelerates uniformly at 2 m/s². The distance travelled by the car in the 5<sup>th</sup> second is:","o":["9 m","10 m","16 m","25 m"],"a":0,"x":"Distance in the n<sup>th</sup> second: s<sub>n</sub> = u + a(2n − 1)/2 = 0 + 2(2·5 − 1)/2 = <b>9 m</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Units & Dimensions","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The dimensional formula of Planck’s constant (h) is:","o":["[M L² T⁻²]","[M L² T⁻¹]","[M L T⁻¹]","[M L⁻² T⁻¹]"],"a":1,"x":"E = hν ⇒ h = E/ν. [E] = M L² T⁻² and [ν] = T⁻¹, so [h] = <b>M L² T⁻¹</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Kinematics","lv":2,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"A projectile is launched at 45° to the horizontal with a speed of 20 m/s. Taking g = 10 m/s², its maximum height is:","o":["5 m","10 m","20 m","40 m"],"a":1,"x":"H = u² sin²θ / (2g) = (400 × ½) / 20 = <b>10 m</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Work, Energy & Power","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"A 4 kg block at rest on a smooth horizontal surface is pulled by a constant horizontal force of 8 N through a distance of 9 m. Its final speed is:","o":["3 m/s","6 m/s","9 m/s","12 m/s"],"a":1,"x":"Work done W = F·d = 8 × 9 = 72 J = ½mv² = 2v² ⇒ v² = 36 ⇒ <b>v = 6 m/s</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Electrostatics","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"Two point charges of 2 μC and 3 μC are placed 3 cm apart in vacuum. The magnitude of the force between them is (1/4πε₀ = 9 × 10⁹ N m² C⁻²):","o":["0.6 N","6 N","60 N","600 N"],"a":2,"x":"F = kq₁q₂/r² = (9×10⁹ × 2×10⁻⁶ × 3×10⁻⁶) / (3×10⁻²)² = 5.4×10⁻² / 9×10⁻⁴ = <b>60 N</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Current Electricity","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"Three resistors of 2 Ω, 3 Ω and 6 Ω are connected in parallel. The equivalent resistance is:","o":["0.5 Ω","1 Ω","2 Ω","11 Ω"],"a":1,"x":"1/R = 1/2 + 1/3 + 1/6 = 3/6 + 2/6 + 1/6 = 1 ⇒ <b>R = 1 Ω</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Ray Optics","lv":2,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"An object is placed 30 cm in front of a convex lens of focal length 20 cm. The image is formed at a distance of:","o":["12 cm","30 cm","50 cm","60 cm"],"a":3,"x":"Lens formula 1/v − 1/u = 1/f with u = −30 cm, f = 20 cm: 1/v = 1/20 − 1/30 = 1/60 ⇒ <b>v = 60 cm</b> (real image on the other side)."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Kinematics","lv":1,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"A stone is dropped from a height of 80 m. Taking g = 10 m/s², the time taken (in seconds) to reach the ground is ______.","a":4,"x":"h = ½gt² ⇒ 80 = 5t² ⇒ t² = 16 ⇒ <b>t = 4 s</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Waves","lv":1,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"A wave has a frequency of 50 Hz and a wavelength of 4 m. Its speed (in m/s) is ______.","a":200,"x":"v = fλ = 50 × 4 = <b>200 m/s</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Heat & Thermodynamics","lv":1,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"The heat required (in kJ) to raise the temperature of 2 kg of water from 20 °C to 70 °C is ______. (Specific heat of water = 4200 J kg⁻¹ K⁻¹)","a":420,"x":"Q = mcΔT = 2 × 4200 × 50 = 4,20,000 J = <b>420 kJ</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Mole Concept","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The number of moles in 11 g of CO₂ is (atomic masses: C = 12, O = 16):","o":["0.25","0.5","1","2"],"a":0,"x":"Molar mass of CO₂ = 44 g/mol, so n = 11 / 44 = <b>0.25 mol</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Periodic Table","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"Which of the following elements has the highest electronegativity?","o":["Chlorine","Oxygen","Fluorine","Nitrogen"],"a":2,"x":"Electronegativity increases across a period and decreases down a group. <b>Fluorine</b> (3.98 on the Pauling scale) is the most electronegative element."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Chemical Bonding","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The hybridisation of the carbon atoms in ethene (C₂H₄) is:","o":["sp","sp²","sp³","sp³d"],"a":1,"x":"Each carbon forms three σ bonds (two C–H and one C–C) and one π bond, so it is <b>sp²</b> hybridised."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Ionic Equilibrium","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The pH of a 0.001 M aqueous solution of HCl is:","o":["1","2","3","11"],"a":2,"x":"HCl is a strong acid, so [H⁺] = 10⁻³ M and pH = −log(10⁻³) = <b>3</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Redox Reactions","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The oxidation state of manganese in KMnO₄ is:","o":["+2","+4","+6","+7"],"a":3,"x":"(+1) + x + 4(−2) = 0 ⇒ x = <b>+7</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Organic Chemistry Basics","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The IUPAC name of CH₃CH₂CH₂OH is:","o":["Propan-2-ol","Propan-1-ol","Propanal","Propanone"],"a":1,"x":"A three-carbon chain with the –OH group on carbon 1 is named <b>propan-1-ol</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Ionic Equilibrium","lv":2,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"Which of the following is a Lewis acid?","o":["NH₃","OH⁻","BF₃","H₂O"],"a":2,"x":"A Lewis acid accepts an electron pair. <b>BF₃</b> has an incomplete octet on boron and readily accepts a pair; NH₃, OH⁻ and H₂O are electron-pair donors."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Mole Concept","lv":1,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"The number of moles of water in 180 g of water is ______. (Molar mass of H₂O = 18 g/mol)","a":10,"x":"n = 180 / 18 = <b>10 mol</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Chemical Bonding","lv":2,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"The total number of σ bonds in a molecule of ethene (C₂H₄) is ______.","a":5,"x":"Four C–H σ bonds + one C–C σ bond (the second C–C bond is a π bond) = <b>5</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Solutions","lv":1,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"20 g of NaOH is dissolved in water to make 250 mL of solution. Its molarity (in mol/L) is ______. (Molar mass of NaOH = 40 g/mol)","a":2,"x":"n = 20 / 40 = 0.5 mol; V = 0.25 L; M = 0.5 / 0.25 = <b>2 mol/L</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","cbse","isc"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Quadratic Equations","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"If α and β are the roots of x² − 5x + 6 = 0, then α² + β² equals:","o":["5","11","13","25"],"a":2,"x":"α + β = 5 and αβ = 6, so α² + β² = (α + β)² − 2αβ = 25 − 12 = <b>13</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","cbse","isc"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Integral Calculus","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The value of ∫<sub>0</sub><sup>π</sup> sin x dx is:","o":["0","1","2","π"],"a":2,"x":"[−cos x] from 0 to π = −cos π + cos 0 = 1 + 1 = <b>2</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","cbse","isc"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Probability","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"Two fair dice are thrown. The probability that the sum of the numbers on them is 7 is:","o":["1/12","1/6","5/36","7/36"],"a":1,"x":"Favourable outcomes: (1,6), (2,5), (3,4), (4,3), (5,2), (6,1) = 6 out of 36, so P = <b>1/6</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","cbse","isc"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Sequences & Series","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The 5<sup>th</sup> term of the geometric progression 3, 6, 12, … is:","o":["24","30","48","96"],"a":2,"x":"a = 3, r = 2. T₅ = ar⁴ = 3 × 16 = <b>48</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","cbse","isc"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Coordinate Geometry","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The distance between the points (1, 2) and (4, 6) is:","o":["√7","5","7","25"],"a":1,"x":"d = √[(4 − 1)² + (6 − 2)²] = √(9 + 16) = <b>5</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","cbse","isc"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Coordinate Geometry","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The slope of the line 3x − 4y + 8 = 0 is:","o":["−4/3","−3/4","3/4","4/3"],"a":2,"x":"Rewrite as y = (3/4)x + 2, so the slope is <b>3/4</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","cbse","isc"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Differential Calculus","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The value of d/dx (x³ + sin x) at x = 0 is:","o":["0","1","2","3"],"a":1,"x":"d/dx (x³ + sin x) = 3x² + cos x. At x = 0 this equals 0 + 1 = <b>1</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Sequences & Series","lv":1,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"The sum of the first 20 natural numbers is ______.","a":210,"x":"S = n(n + 1)/2 = 20 × 21 / 2 = <b>210</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Permutations & Combinations","lv":1,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"The number of ways of selecting 2 students from a group of 5 students is ______.","a":10,"x":"⁵C₂ = 5! / (2! · 3!) = <b>10</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Vectors","lv":2,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"If <b>a</b> and <b>b</b> are perpendicular vectors with |<b>a</b>| = 3 and |<b>b</b>| = 4, then |<b>a</b> + <b>b</b>|² equals ______.","a":25,"x":"|a + b|² = |a|² + |b|² + 2 a·b = 9 + 16 + 0 = <b>25</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Circular Motion","lv":2,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"A particle moves along a circle of radius 2 m with a constant speed of 4 m/s. The magnitude of its acceleration is:","o":["2 m/s²","4 m/s²","8 m/s²","16 m/s²"],"a":2,"x":"In uniform circular motion the acceleration is centripetal: a = v²/r = 16/2 = <b>8 m/s²</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Electrostatics","lv":2,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"Two identical capacitors, each of capacitance C, are connected in series across a battery of emf V. The total energy stored is:","o":["CV²/8","CV²/4","CV²/2","CV²"],"a":1,"x":"In series C<sub>eq</sub> = C/2, so U = ½ C<sub>eq</sub> V² = ½ (C/2) V² = <b>CV²/4</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Laws of Motion","lv":2,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"A block on a rough inclined plane of angle θ is just on the verge of sliding down. The coefficient of static friction is:","o":["sin θ","cos θ","tan θ","cot θ"],"a":2,"x":"At the verge of sliding: mg sin θ = μ mg cos θ ⇒ <b>μ = tan θ</b>."},{"ex":["ja"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Heat & Thermodynamics","lv":3,"t":"multi","src":"practice","q":"An ideal gas expands isothermally. Which of the following statements is/are correct?","o":["Its internal energy remains constant","The heat absorbed equals the work done by the gas","The temperature of the gas increases","The pressure of the gas decreases"],"a":[0,1,3],"x":"Isothermal ⇒ ΔT = 0 ⇒ ΔU = 0 for an ideal gas (A). From the first law Q = ΔU + W = W (B). The temperature is constant, so (C) is false. PV = constant, so as V increases P decreases (D). Correct: <b>A, B, D</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Current Electricity","lv":1,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"A 60 W bulb is used for 5 hours every day for 30 days. The energy consumed (in kWh) is ______.","a":9,"x":"E = 0.06 kW × 5 h × 30 = <b>9 kWh</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Physics","ch":"Current Electricity","lv":2,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"Resistors of 4 Ω and 12 Ω are connected in parallel across a 12 V battery. The total current drawn from the battery (in A) is ______.","a":4,"x":"I₁ = 12/4 = 3 A and I₂ = 12/12 = 1 A. Total current = <b>4 A</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Chemical Bonding","lv":2,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The shape of the XeF₄ molecule is:","o":["Tetrahedral","See-saw","Square planar","Octahedral"],"a":2,"x":"Xe has 4 bond pairs and 2 lone pairs (sp³d², octahedral electron geometry). The two lone pairs sit opposite each other, giving a <b>square planar</b> shape."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Periodic Table","lv":2,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"Among Li, Be, B and C, the element with the highest first ionisation enthalpy is:","o":["Li","Be","B","C"],"a":3,"x":"Approximate values (kJ mol⁻¹): Li 520 &lt; B 801 &lt; Be 900 &lt; C 1086. Carbon is highest."},{"ex":["jm","ja","neet","cbse","isc"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Chemical Kinetics","lv":2,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"For a first-order reaction, the half-life is:","o":["Directly proportional to the initial concentration","Independent of the initial concentration","Inversely proportional to the initial concentration","Proportional to the square of the initial concentration"],"a":1,"x":"For a first-order reaction t<sub>½</sub> = 0.693 / k, and k is a constant. So the half-life is <b>independent of the initial concentration</b>."},{"ex":["ja"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"p-Block Elements","lv":3,"t":"multi","src":"practice","q":"Which of the following oxides are amphoteric?","o":["Al₂O₃","ZnO","Na₂O","CO₂"],"a":[0,1],"x":"Al₂O₃ and ZnO react with both acids and bases, so they are amphoteric. Na₂O is basic and CO₂ is acidic. Correct: <b>A, B</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"d-Block Elements","lv":2,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"The number of unpaired electrons in Fe³⁺ (atomic number of Fe = 26) is ______.","a":5,"x":"Fe³⁺ has the configuration [Ar] 3d⁵. By Hund’s rule each of the five d orbitals holds one electron, so there are <b>5</b> unpaired electrons."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Chemistry","ch":"Chemical Bonding","lv":2,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"The number of lone pairs of electrons on the central atom of XeF₂ is ______.","a":3,"x":"Xenon has 8 valence electrons. Two are used to bond with the two F atoms, leaving 6 electrons = <b>3 lone pairs</b> (linear, sp³d)."},{"ex":["jm","ja","cbse","isc"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Limits & Continuity","lv":1,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"lim<sub>x→0</sub> (sin 3x) / x equals:","o":["0","1","3","1/3"],"a":2,"x":"(sin 3x)/x = 3 · (sin 3x)/(3x) → 3 × 1 = <b>3</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","cbse","isc"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Quadratic Equations","lv":3,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The number of real solutions of the equation |x| = x² − 2 is:","o":["1","2","3","4"],"a":1,"x":"For x ≥ 0: x² − x − 2 = 0 ⇒ (x − 2)(x + 1) = 0 ⇒ x = 2 (x = −1 rejected). For x &lt; 0: x² + x − 2 = 0 ⇒ (x + 2)(x − 1) = 0 ⇒ x = −2 (x = 1 rejected). Two solutions: x = ±2, so the answer is <b>2</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja","cbse","isc"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Conic Sections","lv":2,"t":"mcq","src":"practice","q":"The eccentricity of the ellipse x²/25 + y²/9 = 1 is:","o":["3/5","4/5","5/4","1/5"],"a":1,"x":"a² = 25, b² = 9 ⇒ e = √(1 − b²/a²) = √(16/25) = <b>4/5</b>."},{"ex":["ja"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Limits & Continuity","lv":3,"t":"multi","src":"practice","q":"Which of the following functions are continuous at x = 0?","o":["f(x) = |x|","f(x) = x sin(1/x) for x ≠ 0, and f(0) = 0","f(x) = 1/x for x ≠ 0, and f(0) = 0","f(x) = sin x"],"a":[0,1,3],"x":"|x| and sin x are continuous everywhere. For x sin(1/x): |x sin(1/x)| ≤ |x| → 0, so the limit equals f(0) = 0. For 1/x the limit does not exist, so it is discontinuous at 0. Correct: <b>A, B, D</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Sequences & Series","lv":2,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"The sum of the infinite series 1 + 1/3 + 1/9 + 1/27 + … is ______. (Enter as a decimal.)","a":1.5,"x":"Geometric series with a = 1 and r = 1/3: S = a / (1 − r) = 1 / (2/3) = 3/2 = <b>1.5</b>."},{"ex":["jm","ja"],"s":"Mathematics","ch":"Permutations & Combinations","lv":2,"t":"num","src":"practice","q":"The number of distinct arrangements of the letters of the word LEVEL is ______.","a":30,"x":"Five letters with L repeated twice and E repeated twice: 5! / (2! · 2!) = 120 / 4 = <b>30</b>."}];

