em('Introduction to Microeconomics',1,'A Production Possibility Curve (PPC) is concave to the origin because of:',['Constant opportunity cost','Increasing marginal opportunity cost','Decreasing marginal opportunity cost','Zero opportunity cost'],1,'The PPC is concave because as more of one good is produced, resources less suited to it must be used, causing the <b>marginal opportunity cost to increase</b>.');
em('Theory of Demand',1,'When the price of a good falls and, as a result, the quantity demanded of that same good rises, this is called:',['Increase in demand','Expansion in demand','Decrease in demand','Contraction in demand'],1,'A rise in quantity demanded purely due to a fall in the good\'s own price (other factors constant) is called an <b>expansion in demand</b>, a movement along the same demand curve.');
em('Theory of Demand',2,'If the demand for a good is price inelastic, a rise in its price will lead to:',['A fall in total revenue','A rise in total revenue','No change in total revenue','Total revenue becoming zero'],1,'When demand is inelastic, quantity demanded falls proportionately less than the price rise, so total revenue (Price × Quantity) <b>rises</b>.');
em('National Income',1,'Which of the following is included while calculating National Income?',['Sale of second-hand goods','Winning a lottery','Payment for services of a doctor','Gift received from a relative'],2,'Only payments for <b>currently produced goods and services</b> (like a doctor\'s service) are included in national income. Second-hand sales, lottery winnings, and gifts are transfer payments/not current production.');
em('Money and Banking',1,'The primary function of a central bank (like the RBI) is to:',['Accept deposits from the public directly','Act as the currency authority and banker to the government','Provide loans to individual consumers','Sell shares in the stock market'],1,'The central bank\'s core function is being the <b>sole currency authority</b> and banker to the government and other banks, not dealing directly with the general public like a commercial bank.');
em('Government Budget',2,'A budget in which government expenditure exceeds government receipts is called:',['Balanced budget','Surplus budget','Deficit budget','Zero budget'],2,'When expenditure &gt; receipts, it is called a <b>deficit budget</b>; the government needs to borrow to cover the gap.');
